    "['xconnect [peer_ip_address] [vc_id] pw-class [pw_class_name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces se-1/0/2:1 unit 0 family ccc', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `xconnect` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces se-1/0/2:1 unit 0 family ccc\\nset protocols l2circuit interface se-1/0/2:1 neighbor 192.168.3.3 virtual-circuit-id 200\\nset protocols l2circuit interface se-1/0/2:1 encapsulation-type ethernet\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The first command configures the serial interface for CCC (Circuit Cross Connect)\\n2. The second command establishes the L2VPN pseudowire connection to neighbor 192.168.3.3 with VC ID 200\\n3. The third command sets the encapsulation type (though Ethernet is default, it\\'s good practice to specify)\\n\\nNote: Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct \"pw-class\" equivalent - the pseudowire characteristics would typically be configured under the `[edit protocols l2circuit]` hierarchy.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces se-1/0/2:1 unit 0 family ccc'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols l2circuit interface se-1/0/2:1 neighbor 192.168.3.3 virtual-circuit-id 200', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `xconnect` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces se-1/0/2:1 unit 0 family ccc\\nset protocols l2circuit interface se-1/0/2:1 neighbor 192.168.3.3 virtual-circuit-id 200\\nset protocols l2circuit interface se-1/0/2:1 encapsulation-type ethernet\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The first command configures the serial interface for CCC (Circuit Cross Connect)\\n2. The second command establishes the L2VPN pseudowire connection to neighbor 192.168.3.3 with VC ID 200\\n3. The third command sets the encapsulation type (though Ethernet is default, it\\'s good practice to sp